[interviewer · RECOMMENDATION · 8:03] Understood. Beyond what we've discussed, what else could Brew & Bean do to reverse this decline?

[candidate · 9:27] Raising prices seems like the obvious one, since they haven't moved in two years and competitors are probably facing the same bean costs. Beyond that — maybe locking in longer contracts with coffee suppliers so they're not exposed to the spot price. They buy for 200 stores, so there should be some buying power there.

Could also look at the menu mix — push drinks that use less of the expensive inputs, or smaller sizes. And overhead crept up 2 points, which isn't the main story but it's still a few million dollars.

Honestly I'd want to know how much they'd lose in customers if they raised prices, but I don't think I have that.
