[interviewer · RECOMMENDATION · 12:35] Okay. Your latte example assumes volume holds, and you mentioned you don't know how customers would react. How would you decide whether the phased approach is the right call versus a single larger increase?

[candidate · 14:05] I'd test it. Pick maybe 20 stores across different markets, do 10% in some and something steeper in others, run it a few months and compare transaction counts against the stores that didn't change. If volume barely moves in the steeper group, go faster everywhere; if it drops, you've only hurt a handful of stores.

A couple of things I'd want to see before deciding — whether competitors have already raised their prices, because if they have, we're under-priced and the risk is lower. And whether a lot of revenue comes from regulars or loyalty members, since those people probably tolerate a rise better than walk-ins.

Honestly, I'd lean phased just because a 24% jump all at once is the kind of thing that makes the news.
